      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ أَرْمِي بِسَهْمٍ فَلاَ أَدْرِي أَ سَمَّيْتُ أَمْ لَمْ أُسَمِّ فَقَالَ \"كُلْ وَ لاَ بَأْسَ \" فَقُلْتُ أَرْمِي فَيَغِيبُ عَنِّي فَأَجِدُ سَهْمِي فِيهِ فَقَالَ \"كُلْ مَا لَمْ يُؤْكَلْ مِنْهُ وَ إِنْ أُكِلَ مِنْهُ فَلاَ تَأْكُلْ\" مِنْهُ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4129 - Aban ibn Uthman narrated from Isa al-Qummi who said:\nI said to Abu Abdullah (as): \"I shoot an arrow, but I do not know whether I mentioned the name of Allah (swt) (Bismillah) or not.\"\nImam (as) said: \"Eat, and there is no problem.\"\nI said: \"I shoot, and it disappears from my sight, then I find my arrow in it.\"\nImam (as) said: \"Eat as long as nothing has been eaten from it. But if something has been eaten from it, then do not eat it.\""
        ]
      }
    },
